# SES Kit Layout

This repository is the **SES kit** (not a home for product apps):

```text
standards/           # shared engineering standards (source of truth)
.cursor/rules/       # Cursor rules for kit development
.cursor/skills/      # feature-planning, feature-implementation, independent-review
skeleton/            # universal product skeleton + modules
templates/           # product-facing Cursor templates for `ses setup`
packages/ses-cli/    # ses init, ses setup, ses check (pip: ses-cli)
docs/                # setup, questionnaire, publishing, pilot lessons
```

- Real products are **separate repos**. Scaffold with `ses init` in the product cwd; refresh Cursor kit with `ses setup`.
- Do not nest apps under a kit `products/` folder for normal use.
- Kit rules/skills live under `.cursor/` so Cursor discovers them while developing SES itself.
- Do not create cloud resources, commit secrets, or overwrite a non-empty product cwd without explicit `--force`.
